class.description:
[InputActionRebinder] is the "press a key now" flow of a rebinding menu. [method begin] picks an action and an event index, the menu forwards its input events to [method update], and the first usable event is bound at once through [InputMapSettingsServer]. Mouse motion, released keys and buttons, echo events, weak stick moves and a modifier key pressed on its own are not used. The event is stored like the server stores it (a pressed key by its physical keycode, a stick by its axis and direction, for all devices), so it is exactly what a save and load of the settings gives back.
If another action already uses the event, [member conflict_mode] decides: ask the menu ([constant CONFLICT_ASK], the default), refuse and wait for another input, swap the two events, or allow both actions to use it. Conflicts are looked up in the merged [InputMap]: the built-in and the custom actions, with the pending events of the actions that [InputMapSettingsServer] stores. Only events of the device class of [member device_filter] are compared.
The signals of this class describe the flow ([signal started], [signal conflict], [signal completed], [signal canceled]). The new events themselves are announced by the server: [signal InputMapSettingsServer.action_events_changed] is emitted for every action that changed (both actions on a swap) before [signal completed]. There is no built-in cancel key, because Escape can be a binding; the menu calls [method cancel].
Several rebinders can run at the same time, for example one per player in local co-op with [member device_filter] [constant DEVICE_GAMEPAD] and their own [member gamepad_device]. Use it from the main thread.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var rebinder := InputActionRebinder.new()

func _ready():
	rebinder.device_filter = InputActionRebinder.DEVICE_KEYBOARD_MOUSE
	rebinder.completed.connect(func(action, index, event): print("%s: %s" % [action, InputMapSettingsServer.get_event_label(event)]))

func _on_jump_button_pressed():
	rebinder.begin(&"jump", 0)

func _input(event):
	if rebinder.update(event):
		get_viewport().set_input_as_handled()
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
private InputActionRebinder _rebinder = new InputActionRebinder();

public override void _Ready()
{
	_rebinder.DeviceFilter = InputActionRebinder.DeviceFilterEnum.KeyboardMouse;
	_rebinder.Completed += (action, index, @event) => GD.Print($"{action}: {InputMapSettingsServer.GetEventLabel(@event)}");
}

private void OnJumpButtonPressed()
{
	_rebinder.Begin("jump", 0);
}

public override void _Input(InputEvent @event)
{
	if (_rebinder.Update(@event))
	{
		GetViewport().SetInputAsHandled();
	}
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
